{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The summary.json file is unusually large because it embeds environment witnesses.\n\nThe review will independently verify the executor's self-check rather than accepting it at face value. Four specific areas require inspection: leftover configuration consumers, native Laravel UUIDv7 implementation, ResourceId transport logic, and BC deltas in approved-deltas.json.\n\nAdditional review areas include deterministic DDL, package boundaries, tests and retired mutation inventory, the PHPStan baseline reduction to exactly 18 blocks, CRM string return types, and HasUuids behavior. The Laravel version must be verified to ensure native UUIDv7 is active and that newUniqueId was not overridden. Models that still lack HasUuids also need to be identified.\n\nThe review will also hunt for models that still use incrementing integer keys instead of UUIDs. The User model exception must be verified: tenant users may retain external identity projection semantics rather than generating their own IDs. Hidden config() calls in migrations, mismatched BC approvals, leftover fromConfigured aliases, forbidden ResourceIdFormat backing values, wire format changes, sabotage mutation patches, and stale documentation references are additional targets.\n\nThe HasUuids trait may not produce UUIDv7 if the Laravel version or an override changes the generation logic.\n\nCoreOptions constructor positional BC must be checked against 13 comparisons.\n\nResolvesCoreOptions removal requires verification against D117. If it was in the accepted stable base, a removal row is mandatory. The self-check claims zero actual stable Roave rows. This claim must be validated against evidence.\n\nThe snapshot likely lacks the accepted stable base revision source. I will inspect approved-deltas and the V17 log to see what Roave actually reported. I must not invent removed-surface BC rows absent from the actual accepted base.\n\nA validation evidence gap surfaced: V14 maps to a rebaseline format folder, which is suspicious. The review will also hunt for semantic issues that gates may have missed.\n\nV14 is mislabeled in the validation evidence. The result path `054-affected-rebaseline-format` belongs to a rebaseline format gate, not the anti-weakening gate. This means V14 may have never run as intended. The self-check incorrectly attributes that output to V14. I will inspect `054/result.json` to confirm whether the anti-weakening gate was actually executed.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The executor’s self-check is not evidence. I am checking the product and the actual gate logs for leftover configuration, BC admissions, UUIDv7 behavior, and whether every required check really ran."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-99394aef-92fe-416d-8f8a-d1bb5738120e-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\"id\"|\"command\"|\"exit\"|\"status\"|\"expected\"","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/validation","glob":"**/result.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-99394aef-92fe-416d-8f8a-d1bb5738120e-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"IdStrategy|HasConfiguredId|IdColumns|idStrategy|ids\\.strategy|corex\\.tables|fromConfigured|ResolvesCoreOptions|HasUuids|uniqueIds|newUniqueId","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/product","glob":"*.{php,md,json,neon,txt,sh}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-99394aef-92fe-416d-8f8a-d1bb5738120e-16","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"config\\(|app\\(CoreOptions|getTable\\(","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/product","glob":"**/database/migrations/**/*.php"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31266,"output_tokens":1395,"cache_read_input_tokens":67328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b4e55ca-100b-4ffe-b286-487065692f9c","uuid":"3fa071df-6088-41b0-8200-ee2a1d86e87e"}
