{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_7","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The mutation-all test completed in only 12 seconds. This is flagged as a potential issue.\n\nThe mutation log is massive and likely compressed into a single line. I will grep it for PASS/FAIL markers and case names.\n\nCustom-fields BC shows \"compatible\" status. The Options tables may have been excluded from the public stable API, or the change was backward-compatible.\n\nCore BC reports 90 changes detected. The self-check indicates 45 core changes and 10 operations rows.\n\nRoave appears to double-count errors across comparison modes. The 45 core and 10 operations rows match the self-check.\n\nHowever, many core errors are actually P08.1 deltas rather than P08.2 changes. These include removed schema version constants and added error codes. They were already approved in the base commit.\n\nThe core stable base is commit 1734ce24185a1adf7abb8fef36d37439c7357f25. Roave compares against this published stable base, so it includes all unpublished deltas since that point, not just P08.2.\n\nD103 requires approving only declared constructor delta rows, not blanket entries. The approved-deltas.json must therefore cover every Roave error since the stable base, including prior P08.1 items that were already approved, plus any new P08.2 rows. Adding P08.2 rows while preserving existing entries is correct under this rule.\n\nResolvesCoreOptions is absent from the core Roave error list. The log shows only deletions for HasConfiguredId, IdColumns, and IdStrategy. This class was likely not in the stable public API surface that Roave scans. D117 requires an actual Roave row, so omitting it is correct. The self-check flags this as absent from the accepted stable base.\n\nI need to verify whether ResolvesCoreOptions was marked @Api or @Spi. If it was SPI, Roave would not scan it, so its absence from the error list is expected. D117 requires an actual Roave row for admission, so fabricating one would be incorrect. I must check if it was a public symbol in the golden baseline.\n\nResourceIdFormat class additions are unlikely to be flagged as BC breaks by Roave. The operations errors are four P08.2 resource id changes, each duplicated, plus pre-existing items such as ApiOptions, AcceptNegotiation, and error codes.\n\nThe 10 operations rows likely represent the full historical count for that package, not merely new P08.2 changes. The approval file must therefore cover every current Roave error for both core and operations, not just P08.2 deltas.\n\nI still need to inspect CustomFieldsOptions to understand why removing its public table fields produced no BC break.\n\nI will inspect the source files and approved-deltas structure to understand why custom-fields remained compatible despite table removals.\n\nI also need to grep the mutation log for test results.\n\nI must verify that HasUuids implements UUIDv7 by examining Laravel's source code.\n\nThe User model does not appear to use HasUuids.\n\nThe self-check confirms the Tenant User retains external identity projection semantics. I need to inspect the diff to verify whether User.php previously used HasConfiguredId.\n\nI will search the diff for all model changes to ensure none lost HasConfiguredId without gaining HasUuids. The specification requires 34 such updates.\n\nI also need to check for integer id columns that should have become UUID, any remaining ULID references, and IdColumns usage.\n\nRemaining config keys in corex.php need verification. ResourceId implementation correctness and audit writer behavior require inspection. Phpstan baseline counts and mutation script retirement status must be checked. Models extending BaseModel inherit HasUuids automatically, so models outside that hierarchy must explicitly use the trait. Models extending BaseModel while also using HasUuids redundantly are harmless.\n\nLaravel's HasUuids trait overrides model properties through methods. If a model extends BaseModel and sets `$incrementing` or `$keyType` as properties, the trait's `getIncrementing()` and `getKeyType()` methods take precedence. This prevents accidental integer key generation on UUID models.\n\nI need to verify the vendored HasUuids.php against Laravel 13.34 to confirm it returns UUIDv7 strings.\n\nD117 requires Model::performInsert to call setUniqueIds before model events, including during saveQuietly. The audit writer should therefore rely on saveQuietly without manual ID assignment.\n\nI will read DatabaseSynchronousAuditWriter and its test to confirm this behavior.\n\nThe full ResourceId file and the BC approved-deltas structure also require inspection.\n\nI should check for leftover consumers of removed config keys such as corex.ids that the V1 pattern might have missed.\n\nI will inspect docs/reference/public-api.md for stale references to removed symbols. I also need to review mutation-check.sh to confirm retired cases and verify surviving patches do not target removed code.\n\nP1.19-drop-precision.patch and P1.23-stale-read.patch were modified. D116 requires reanchoring surviving patches without altering sabotage intent, so I will inspect their diffs to confirm the original sabotage intent remains intact.\n\nThe schema comparison already shows all checks pass, including columns, constraints, indexes, and pg_dump. I will still spot-check the catalog for UUID column drift versus integer columns and verify that the default catalog was retained.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c97c1b76-14b9-4278-92b2-3f9524d10ed1-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/validation/schema-before/summary.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c97c1b76-14b9-4278-92b2-3f9524d10ed1-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/validation/schema-after/comparison-central.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c97c1b76-14b9-4278-92b2-3f9524d10ed1-32","name":"read_fil