{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_8","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The mutation log appears authentic. Tests fail under sabotage.\n\nThe 12.46-second runtime is plausible. I will verify schema hashes and compare BC approvals against Roave errors. I also plan to inspect approved-deltas.json for P08.2 core and operations entries.\n\nResolvesCoreOptions is absent from the Roave core error JSON. This supports the executor's claim of zero stable rows. The custom-fields table removal must also be checked for public API regressions.\n\nCustomFieldsOptions may not be public, since Roave logged it as compatible. I will read that class to confirm.\n\nUuid and Uuid7 both wire to 'uuid'. D116 expects wire tags like 'uuid|ulid|integer'. I need to verify this preserves the previous Uuid7 semantics.\n\nI will check complete-product.diff for the old ResourceId and deleted IdStrategy. fromConfigured must be absent everywhere. I will read User.php and audit BaseModel and the writer. CoreOptions lost thirteen leading promoted parameters, matching the Dossier's Roave expectation of thirteen property removals.\n\nThe thirteen removed properties caused cascading positional shifts. Parameter types changed for tenantContextResolver and impersonationService.\n\nThe thirteen parameter shifts are now fully enumerated. They include auditLogger, auditRetention, settingDefaultsProvider, departmentRepository, dataScopeAuthorizer, storageDurableRoot, storageEphemeralRoot, viewsConnection, auditEnabled, and settingsCacheTtl. P08.1 leftovers remain approved: two SCHEMA_VERSION constants were removed and five CoreErrorCode cases were added.\n\nHasConfiguredId and bootHasConfiguredId were deleted. IdColumns and IdStrategy were also removed. getKeyType, getIncrementing, newUniqueId, and uniqueIds each appear twice in the Roave log, once as a covariant return type change and once as a non-covariant change. This yields eight return