grations replaced uuid() helpers with literal uuid columns, and confirm schema-after was built from the candidate rather than the baseline.\n\nI will read the central run log. I also need to audit migrations for leftover `$table->ulid()`, `IdColumns`, and `foreignId` calls. The V2 regex may miss spacing variants like `config (` or `CoreOptions::`. I will search the product for any remaining reads of removed options.\n\nI will inspect AttributeCompositionRegistrar, CoreOptions, and the parser for leftover custom-fields references. I also need to audit configuration.md and public-api.md for stale keys.\n\nCore zone tests changed. I must verify these changes did not weaken package boundaries.\n\nThe anti-weakening log shows SQLite dropped by two tests and PostgreSQL by eight. I will read anti-weakening-allowances.txt and the deleted test inventory to confirm these allowances match the retired set exactly.\n\nI am verifying that the deleted test counts match the anti-weakening allowances exactly. The SQLite allowance of -2 likely covers ConfigurableIdTest.php, and the PostgreSQL allowance of -8 likely covers UlidGenerationTest plus additional tests. I must confirm no other tests were removed beyond what these allowances permit.\n\nThe gate passed with exactly the permitted deltas. I am now checking whether the deleted ConfigurableIdTest was replaced by a weaker BaseModelIdentityTest that still covers UUIDv7 persistence per D117 and P08.2.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fc90b46a-ddc5-4c51-9917-6b81c8092d01-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fromConfigured|IdStrategy|ResolvesCoreOptions|idStrategy|corex\\.tables|corex-custom-fields\\.tables|settingsTable|HasConfiguredId","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/product","glob":"*.{php,md,json,neon}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fc90b46a-ddc5-4c51-9917-6b81c8092d01-38","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\\$incrementing|keyType|ulid\\(|bigIncrements|foreignId\\(|config\\(|env\\(|CoreOptions|IdColumns","path":"/