{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_12","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Counting core package change rows.\n\nOperations change rows total 10. Core package changes span lines 678 to 898. D117 may appear in core decisions around line 640. Potential real bugs are being examined.\n\nContextGuard::id still accepts string|int, but D117 requires string-only identifiers. CrmIdentifier now returns only strings and rejects non-strings. Need to verify whether CRM still contains integer IDs.\n\nRejecting integers in CrmIdentifier is correct. ConvertLead newUniqueId usage is acceptable. The phpstan baseline needs checking for new ignores. Mutation patches P1.19 and P1.23 require comparison to confirm sabotage changes versus reanchorings. Laravel Model performInsert must be verified for setUniqueIds ordering before events during saveQuietly. HasUniqueStringIds setUniqueIds behavior needs review. User model changes need grep diff inspection. Schema catalog sample comparison for a changed table is also required.\n\nconfiguration-classes.json around line 244 needs inspection for removed keys. ResourceId tests and core zone test changes require review to confirm no weakening. docs/reference/public-api.md must be checked for removed symbols still listed as current and for ResourceIdFormat presence. Custom-fields Options table removal is internal and final, so the Roave-compatible approach is correct. The golden baseline should record this php-surface change despite the internal status. V13 passed.\n\nResolvesCoreOptions may have been an SPI trait in the public PHP API surface. Roave might not flag SPI deletions depending on configuration. The bc-check log contains no ResolvesCoreOptions error, so omitting that row is correct. The V17 log should be grepped to confirm this. Models that previously relied on options for their table name must be checked for missing $table literals.\n\nTests passed, so models likely retain explicit $table names or their pluralized class names match. I will inspect AuditLog, Setting, Department, FeatureFlag, Sprint, Deal, and ContactCompany for literal table assignments. RoleAssignment also needs verification. Migrations require checking consistency between uuid and foreignUuid column declarations.\n\nSqlSavedViewRepository generates UUIDv7 identifiers directly via Str::uuid7(). This is acceptable.\n\nThe P1.23 stale-read patch was modified for the department repository. The re-read guard under lock remains intact at lines 96-102. The patch still targets the guard without weakening the product code.\n\nD116 requires reanchoring without altering the sabotage. The patch diff must be compared to confirm the sabotaged lines retain their original meaning.\n\nD117 mandates exactly 18 removed PHPStan blocks, zero additions, and one CRM argument.type removal. Any new baseline entries added by the diff would violate this rule. The diff will be searched for phpstan-baseline additions.\n\nA grep pattern will locate new PHPStan ignore errors. CoreLitmusTest and CoreZoneTest changes need inspection for weakened assertions. The deleted ConfigurableIdTest must be reviewed to confirm BaseModelIdentityTest preserves the uuid7 contract. A potential ResourceId bug is suspected: Uuid7 and Uuid share wire tag 'uuid', but parse compares wire format with hash_equals against expected format's wire tag.\n\nThe suspected ResourceId bug is resolved. Uuid7 and Uuid share the wire tag 'uuid', but version nibbles distinguish them. When the expected format is Uuid, version 7 is accepted as a generic UUID; when the expected format is Uuid7, other versions are rejected. This matches D116's requirement that both remain supported.\n\nPHP 8.4 on Linux is 64-bit, so integer overflow from filter_var INT max is unlikely. Large integers that fit PostgreSQL bigint but not PHP int would be rejected, though this may be pre-existing rather than a new bug. The canonicalInteger diff needs inspection.\n\nAuthorizationLayersTest around line 141 requires review for resource id tests.\n\nCore models in other packages correctly use Laravel's HasUuids instead of the core IdStrategy.\n\nIt remains to verify whether access package models that are not BaseModel children miss soft deletes or audit behavior.\n\nChecking Invitation, RoleAssignment, and Deal models for custom ID generation and table assignments. Searching configuration-classes.json for ids.strategy or tables entries. Verifying corex.php configuration for removed id and table settings. Grepping php-api.json for ResourceIdFormat, fromConfigured, and fromValue signatures. Confirming ResolvesCoreOptions absence in the golden surface. Checking the mutation log to ensure all 35 items were restored.\n\nChecking mutation log counts for OK, FAIL, and восстанов markers. Comparing schema catalogs for id columns on sys_audit_log and a CRM table. Verifying D22 invariants do not permit configurability. Inspecting core-zones.md around the D116 section to confirm the prompt did not embed product file content.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2fc13ad6-9b81-42f8-9fba-2df9dc70c13b-62","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^diff --git","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/complete-product.diff"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2fc13ad6-9b81-42f8-9fba-2df9dc70c13b-63","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ResolvesCoreOptions|fromConfigured|ResourceIdFormat","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/validation/066-V17-final3/output.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2fc13ad6-9b81-42f8-9fba-2df9dc70c13b-64","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ids\\.strategy|corex\\.tables|custom-fields\\.tables|idStrategy|\"tables\"","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/product/scripts/configuration-classes.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2fc13ad6-9b81-42f8-9fba-2df9dc70c13b-65","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function performInsert|setUniqueIds|saveQuietly","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/dependencies/vendor/laravel/framework/src/Illuminate/D