{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_13","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to examine suspicious diffs more carefully.\n\nI am now reading the smaller suspicious hunks. These include User.php, phpstan baselines, mutation patches, CoreOptions parser, ResourceId wire behavior, Core zone and litmus, Department repository, SqlSavedViewRepository, approved-deltas additions, CRM phpstan, ContextGuard, Deal model, Audit writer, and configuration-classes.\n\ncompany_contact_parity and full_storage_parity diffs are 300 lines each. They may have reformatted or changed more than config-to-literal. The catalog comparison shows schema matches, so the DDL output is unchanged. Source changes are acceptable as long as the catalog result stays the same.\n\nI will spot-check that constraints were not deleted in the large diffs. I am now reading the phpstan baseline suppressions, CoreLitmusTest weakening, NoCrossDbFkTest, and Model performInsert to verify setUniqueIds runs before events.\n\nI am reading Model.php lines 1602-1650 and HasUniqueStringIds to verify setUniqueIds ordering. I will count core BC rows from approved-deltas line 640. D117 may be absent from the decisions list because ResolvesCoreOptions produced zero Roave rows. The HasUuids return type changes are D112 consequential per the dossier. D103 binds admission to the decision.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c9c6fdc6-8e37-4833-b0e8-602b25d28c6f-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/complete-product.diff","offset":741,"limit":140}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c9c6fdc6-8e37-4833-b0e8-602b25d28c6f-67","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/complete-product.diff","offset":4198,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c9c6fdc6-8e37-4833-b0e8-602b25d28c6f-68","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/complete-product.diff","offset":5002,"limit":