{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_16","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ContextGuard::id still accepts string|int.\n\nD117 permits CRM returns to become string or nullable string without altering other boundary checks. The workspace() return was changed from string|int|null to ?string. The id() parameter still accepts int but now validates as UUID only, and the error message changed. This is the direct consequence of removing int and ulid strategies, which is correct for D112.\n\nThe id() parameter retains string|int to avoid a broader signature break. Existing callers passing int still type-check but fail the UUID runtime check. This is slightly loose but not a blocker. It does not constitute a current-scope acceptance failure.\n\nDeal currency PHPDoc now declares `@property string $currency`, removing int from the create() attribute union and dropping the stale baseline. CoreOptions lost 13 change objects in the diff.\n\nCoreOptions changed 13 rows. HasUniqueStringIds and HasUuids each lost 2 return-type rows. BaseModel boot was removed. CoreOptions null handling was removed. IdColumns and IdStrategy null handling were also removed. The diff totals 38 new rows. Seven pre-existing rows remain. This matches the expected baseline.\n\nOperations schema diff adds four rows, bringing the total to ten and matching Roave. No D117 row appears, which is correct.\n\nThe configuration-classes diff must be inspected to confirm only removed keys were deleted and unrelated classes remain intact. The public-api.md, core README, and viewsTable literal usage in SqlSavedViewRepository also need verification. A schema catalog spot check and mutation log review for all thirty-five items are required. V4 output indicates configuration.md was regenerated without IDs. The custom-fields README should be checked for documentation of table removals.\n\nResourceIdFormat correctly resides in the operations package. HasUuids preserves all HasConfiguredId behavior, including key type and incrementing settings. The Setting model correctly omits SoftDeletes and HasAuditLog because it never extended BaseModel. HasUuids properly sets $keyType to string.\n\nAudit log model tests pass without timestamps because HasUuids does not require them. Migrations were scanned for dynamic Schema::connection calls and getTable references, but none were found. The full_storage_parity diff is roughly two hundred lines and likely mechanical replacement; the catalog confirms DDL output is unchanged.\n\nStr::isUuid accepts any UUID version, not only v7. CRM references may be explicit non-v7 UUIDs, and the schema stores them as generic uuid type. This is correct.\n\nD112 mandates UUIDv7 generation but accepts any UUID for validation. Explicit keys in BaseModelIdentityTest already use v7, so this is not a blocker.\n\nPublic API docs still list IdStrategy. I will grep public-api.md, php-surface, and php-api.json to verify whether ResolvesCoreOptions, HasConfiguredId, and other legacy identifiers remain exposed. The core README strategy section also needs inspection. I already confirmed that docs/architecture/configuration.md does not contain corex.ids.\n\nThe scorecard change appears informational. V20 completion notes are absent from the snapshot, but self-check.json and the summary already establish V20 as GREEN. The user requested final check logs and results; V20 is a procedure rather than a command, so the static mapping serves as evidence. I independently verified that mapping is largely accurate.\n\nThe self-check evidence is sufficient, so the review will now hunt for genuine defects. SqlSavedViewRepository::viewsTable needs inspection for literal table references. DatabasePollPubSub and prune commands must be checked for table option replacements. MessagingRegistrar diff requires review. Models that previously inherited $table from HasConfiguredId may now lack it. The deleted HasConfiguredId file also needs boot behavior verification.\n\nConfiguration metadata is internally consistent because V4 passed. Custom-fields tests and access test migrations need inspection for hardcoded table names. Models must be checked for a protected $keyType of 'int' that conflicts with HasUuids. The tenancy NoCrossDbFkTest diff should be reviewed for weakened foreign key checks. CoreOptionsParser correctly lost its table() helper.\n\nDeal correctly omits HasUuids because it extends BaseModel directly. AuditLog previously extended Model and now uses HasUuids; this is pre-existing and acceptable. Subclasses inheriting HasConfiguredId from BaseModel automatically receive HasUuids, so they inherit UUIDv7 generation. The deleted HasConfiguredId file still needs inspection to compare its newUniqueId implementation with Str::uuid7().\n\nThe catalog column type remains uuid, so a generation algorithm change is acceptable under D112. Laravel Str::uuid7() implements RFC 9562 and correctly checks version nibble 7. The mutation log tail needs inspection for restored sources and case counts.\n\nThe P1.19 patch diff reveals the minus context already uses uuid literals, while the plus line drops precision from timestampTz. The sabotage of dropping precision is preserved in the patch file itself.\n\nThe P1.19 patch diff confirms the IdColumns-to-uuid replacement is present, and the precision sabotage line remains intact. The mutation log shows this patch applied cleanly.\n\nThe P1.19 patch applies cleanly and the test fails as intended.\n\nAccess identity table preservation is unverifiable because the access config files are absent from the snapshot. The directory listing shows only composer.json, phpunit.xml, src/Enums, src/Roles, and tests under packages/access/.\n\nThe access config file is absent from the dependency snapshot, so byte-identical verification is impossible. The product change list and diff both omit it, confirming no modification occurred. D112 §2 preservation is satisfied. The azguard table_names file is also unchanged.\n\nThe public-api.md diff needs inspection for incorrect removals or missing ResourceIdFormat. The operations README wire format documentation must be verified. php-api.json needs grepping for ResourceId fromValue signatures. The rename-completeness gate passed because D116 is a type change rather than a class rename.\n\nThe anti-weakening gate shows a net -2 sqlite test reduction. ConfigurableIdTest and UlidGenerationTest were deleted, while BaseModelIdentityTest was added. The allowance text cites retired-test-inventory.json, which is absent from the snapshot.\n\nThe anti-weakening gate passed with exactly the allowances applied. I am now inspecting the deleted test files to verify whether the allowance over-credits by allowing more sqlite test removals than those files actually contain.\n\nI will count the it( and test() calls inside the deleted UlidGenerationTest and ConfigurableIdTest to verify the sqlite test allowance matches the observed drop. I also need to scan surviving test diffs for removed assertions that could weaken coverage beyond the retired inventory.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a17499a6-b564-4b6d-887a-14215108be13-84","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^(it|test)\\(","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/deleted"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a17499a6-b564-4b6d-887a-14215108be13-85","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ResolvesCoreOptions|IdStrategy|HasConfiguredId|fromConfigured|ResourceIdFormat","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/product/docs/reference/public-api.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a17499a6-b564-4b6d-887a-14215108be13-86","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ResolvesCoreOptions|IdStrategy|HasConfiguredId|ResourceIdFormat","path":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/product/packages/core/resources/contracts/php-api.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a17499a6-b564-4b6d-887a-14215108be13-87","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ResolvesCoreOptions|\"IdStrategy\"|HasConfiguredId|ResourceIdForma