{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_17","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"php-api.json for core contains no matches for ResolvesCoreOptions, IdStrategy, HasConfiguredId, or ResourceIdFormat.\n\nResourceIdFormat is correctly located in the operations package rather than core. The golden surface shows ResourceIdFormat and confirms the deleted symbols are absent. ConfigurableIdTest contains eight test calls with a pg allowance of negative eight.\n\nThe anti-weakening gate splits lanes. Some ConfigurableIdTest tests may run on sqlite too, which would inflate the sqlite delta unless they are strictly pg-only. UlidGenerationTest contributes two sqlite tests. The gate observed a sqlite drop of -2 and a pg drop of -8.\n\nThe sqlite removals net to -2. UlidGenerationTest accounts for two removed tests. ConfigurableIdTest contributes one additional sqlite test. BaseModelIdentityTest adds one more sqlite test. The arithmetic balances the observed drop.\n\nThe prior arithmetic is inconsistent. If ConfigurableIdTest contributes zero sqlite tests, the observed sqlite drop of -2 cannot be explained by UlidGenerationTest alone. The remaining possibilities are that BaseModelIdentityTest belongs to a different suite, another sqlite test was removed, or pest datasets were replaced.\n\nConfigurableIdTest may be entirely pg-grouped, which would leave zero sqlite tests and explain the UlidGenerationTest drop alone. The new BaseModelIdentityTest is located at packages/core/tests/Feature/BaseModelIdentityTest.php.\n\nThe anti-weakening gate may only count root-level tests, not package tests. The observed drop of two sqlite tests means removals outnumber additions by exactly two. Ten test functions were deleted from UlidGenerationTest and ConfigurableIdTest combined. Pest datasets multiply test counts, so the actual sqlite total likely exceeds ten.\n\nConfigurableIdTest likely contains pest datasets that multiply the pg test count. The gate counts pest tests directly rather than closures, so the observed pg drop of eight aligns with the allowance. No inconsistency exists between the gate and the allowance.\n\nThe sqlite drop of -2 matches UlidGenerationTest alone if the gate counts only root-level tests. BaseModelIdentityTest is in packages/core/tests, so it would be excluded from the sqlite lane. ConfigurableIdTest would then be entirely pg-grouped, yielding the observed -8 pg drop. The file's pest datasets and group declarations still need verification.\n\nOperations php-api must be checked around line 4359 for the fromValue signature with ResourceIdFormat and the absence of fromConfigured. Core php-api should still contain CoreOptions without idStrategy. The grep for idStrategy found only changelogs and a rebase line. The golden surface lines for ResourceIdFormat enum cases need inspection to confirm backing values.\n\nThe secret classification on `write_tokens` was removed with the tables configuration. This is correct because the key itself was deleted, not a bug. The next concern to inspect is whether `HasUuids` is applied to models with non-uuid or composite primary keys.\n\nThe implementation appears largely correct. A subtle finding is that ContextGuard::id still accepts `int` in its signature, though the underlying boundary check now validates UUIDs rather than strategy matches.\n\nD117 requires CRM methods returning identifiers to return string or nullable string. The workspace() and CrmIdentifier fixes are complete, but other CRM methods may still declare `string|int` or `: int`. A grep of flex-crm is needed to confirm compliance. Core README may still contain a strategy section. Public-api was checked and shows no remaining IdStrategy references.\n\nThe next checks are whether operations php-api still declares fromConfigured, whether ResourceIdFormat carries backing values in the golden surface, and whether AuthorizationLayersTest covers all four formats plus rejection.\n\nA spot check of the sys_settings id column in both schema catalogs will confirm the evidence is real rather than a stub. The environment witness product hash must match. Mutation 35 cases need counting via grep. P1.19-hardcode and P1.20 are confirmed absent from the mutation script with deleted patch files present. The core config diff around lines 257-308 should be inspected to ensure only ids and tables keys were removed. The custom fields options diff needs review for accidental driver removals.\n\nDatabasePollPubSub diffs need inspection for hardcoded table name errors. The Invitation model uses HasUuids on wsp_invitations, and the catalog confirms the migration output unchanged. ConvertLead diff needs review for id generation correctness.\n\nCoreOptionsParser was verified clean; the `$tables` variable and its usages were removed together, so V6 lint passed without errors.\n\nThe PHPStan baseline contains exactly eighteen removal blocks and no additions.\n\nNext checks include flex-crm for remaining `int` returns, operations tests, scorecard/core-zones for false claims, and table literals in `savedViewScopes` and `PruneOutboxMessages`.\n\nThe department repository diff around line 2109 is being checked to confirm only the table name changed and no logic was altered. Messaging diffs are also being reviewed.\n\nThe review will conclude GREEN if no blocker is found. Recommendations for D113 normalization, connection-guard cleanup, and ContextGuard::id typing will be noted as future scope items. D117 §3 applies to CRM returns, not parameter types. The remaining task is to search flex-crm for any other `string|int` return declarations.\n\nThe `id(string|int $id)` parameter is not a blocker. The validation body was correctly updated to UUID-only checks, so rejecting an `int` value is expected behavior. The decision only requires changes to return type declarations, not parameter unions.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4a8b8998-002f-4629-b3c6-d4a3164f3