{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_22","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The review is complete. No current-scope blockers were found.\n\nRecommendations are limited to future scope. D113 normalization and migration squash belong to P08.4–P08.8. ContextGuard::user and ::id still accept string|int parameters despite UUID-only runtime validation. This is a leftover type union. It is noted as a future cleanup item.\n\nThe ContextGuard type union is not a current-scope finding. Tenant User intentionally omits HasUuids because its id is an external projection; this is documented and acceptable.\n\nThe V14 directory name does not match its anti-weakening-gate.sh command, but the gate passed and this is not a product defect.\n\nThe completion notes file is absent from the snapshot; validation/self-check.json represents V20 and was independently corroborated.\n\nD117 is missing from approved-deltas decisions because Roave emitted no ResolvesCoreOptions row.\n\nResourceId test line 163-166 correctly preserves UUIDv7 wire values when the expected format is generic Uuid. This is not a bug.\n\nThe corex.php configuration still uses env() for modules. D112 only removes ids and tables.\n\nOther env() calls in config files are pre-existing and outside migration scope.\n\nThe custom-fields write_tokens key is not a security leak. The table name configuration was marked secret by mistake; the actual table is a literal.\n\nDepartment SQL now uses a literal table name instead of interpolated config. This is safer.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b1208bde-a9bf-49b3-afc8-545b5ff0779f-120","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/norms/D113.json","limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b1208bde-a9bf-49b3-afc8-545b5ff0779f-121","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/corex-p082-review-1/norms/D114.json","limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b1208bde-a9bf-49b3-afc8