{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_23","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 23 PHPStan packages passed.\n\nThe review is GREEN. Findings are empty. Recommendations will be limited to future scope only. Coverage and validation assessments will be brief. A residual ContextGuard string|int issue will be noted as a recommendation.\n\nThe ContextGuard string|int observation will be omitted from recommendations. It does not violate adopted norms, so it is excluded to keep the list strictly limited to deferred work.\n\nContextGuard::user and ::id still accept string|int; runtime UUID checks reject integers. Narrowing those parameters is not required by D117 and can wait.\n\nThe validation assessment will note that bc-check exit 0 proves the SHA-256 hashes and row set match the Roave output without recomputing them.\n\nThe product hash matches all final result files. Schema comparisons across both baselines pass on all eight fields, with 193 columns in the central witness. The review is confirmed GREEN. Only the final JSON object will be returned.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"{\"verdict\":\"GREEN\",\"findings\":[],\"recommendations\":[{\"scope\":\"P08.4–P08.8 / D113\",\"note\":\"Baseline file layout, index names, bigint counters, and polymorphic string pairs stay deferred. P08.2 only freezes the default uuid catalog.\"},{\"scope\":\"P08.5 / P08.10 / D114\",\"note\":\"Signup and cleanup columns that replace root_accounts.data are not part of this item.\"},{\"scope\":\"later CRM typing\",\"note\":\"ContextGuard::user and ContextGuard::id still accept string|int. id() rejects every non-UUID at runtime, and the string|int returns named by D117 are already string. Narrowing those two parameters can wait.\"}],\"coverage\":\"Reviewed the P08.2 snapshot against D112, D116, D117, D103, D22, and the P08.2 spec: removed id/table configuration and its consumers, native HasUuids UUIDv7 including quiet audit insert, operations ResourceIdFormat with unchanged uuid|ulid|integer wire tags and no fromConfigured alias, literal migration DDL, host identity.table and AzGuard table_names left untouched, finite BC approvals, Golden/API surfaces, PHPStan baseline removals, retired tests, and the two obsolete mutation cases. Tenant User keeps an external id and does not generate one. ResolvesCoreOptions is gone from source, php-api, and php-surface; Roave reported no stable row, so no invented approval was required. D111 assigns this item no schema-set work.\",\"validation_assessment\":\"Final logs for candidate 2e909b87 and product sha256 d2817b85ee52fe7b903ef9a67fe468c1422bf8579839b355a63761b1383c1b04 show V1–V19 exit-matched, PHPStan clean, root sqlite 1133 passed, root PG 240 passed, package tests passed, arch 137 passed, golden 4 passed, php-api and bc-check exit 0, and rename-completeness OK. bc-check admitted exactly the emitted stable rows: 45 core (38 new D112 rows plus the prior schema-set rows) and 10 operations (4 new ResourceId rows). Anti-weakening matched the D112 allowances (sqlite 1230→1228, pg 672→664). All 35 surviving mutations failed under sabotage and the tree was restored. Schema witnesses from baseline f6d9e41e and the candidate both compare true on scope, sets, files, migrated objects, columns, constraints, indexes, and pg_dump. Native Redis menu tests passed 4/4 with 29 assertions and no skips. V20 is the supplied self-check mapping; the separate Completion Notes file is outside this snapshot, and the mapping matches the sources above.\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2488,"output_tokens":1258,"cache_read_input_tokens":233216,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b4e55ca-100b-4ffe-b286-487065692f9c","uuid":"92bf5075-aff8-4fc5-a538-1c1e3a90799f"}
